<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Breifne</h1><p class="st-meta">700 CE – 1256 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Gaelic kingdom of the drumlin country of Leitrim and Cavan, ruled by the O'Rourkes, whose king Tigernan Ua Ruairc helped bring about the Norman invasion of 1169.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Breifne emerged in the 8th century among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-briuin">Ui Briuin</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-connacht">Connacht</a>, whose branch, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-briuin-breifne">Ui Briuin Breifne</a>, settled the lakes and hills of later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-leitrim">Leitrim</a> and Cavan. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-ruairc">O'Rourke</a> family became its leading dynasty by the 10th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Breifne was an upland kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, lakes and crannog dwellings. Its kings occasionally claimed the kingship of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-connacht">Connacht</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigernan-ua-ruairc">Tigernan Ua Ruairc</a>, ruler from about 1124 to 1172, fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Leinster</a>, who had abducted his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derbforgaill">Derbforgaill</a>; their feud helped bring the Normans to Ireland. Tigernan was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-of-ward">Tlachtga</a> in 1172.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the death of its king in 1256, Breifne split between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-ruairc">O'Rourkes</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-breifne">West Breifne</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-raghallaigh">O'Reillys</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/east-breifne">East Breifne</a>. Both survived until the late 16th and early 17th centuries.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-breifne.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Breifne" width="320" height="418"><figcaption>Image: Erigena · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Breifne-900.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 CE – 1256 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tigernan Ua Ruairc</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bréifne, Breffny</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=978&amp;focus=kingdom-of-breifne" aria-label="Kingdom of Breifne on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4497 318 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Breifne lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4817 574L4839 583M4817 574L4817 574"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4839 583h0M4817 574h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4817 574h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4817 574h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=978&amp;focus=kingdom-of-breifne">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
